# D-TEST-READS1 (#6064): `jet test` stores a passing run's results with the environment variables its tests read; a rerun with every read variable unchanged reuses them without running the test, and a changed variable runs it again. The test appends to `runs.log` each time it runs.
fixture: test_results_rerun_when_a_read_env_var_changes.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
env: JETPACK_ENV=1
env: TEST_READS_GREETING=hello

step first: jet test
cwd: app
exit: 0
stderr: !~ "reused" # the first run has no stored results
file: app/runs.log = "ran\n"

step again: jet test
cwd: app
exit: 0
stderr: ~ "jet test: reused 1 stored result" # the read variable is unchanged
file: app/runs.log = "ran\n" # so the test did not run

step changed: jet test
cwd: app
env: TEST_READS_GREETING=goodbye
exit: 0
stderr: !~ "reused" # the read variable changed
file: app/runs.log = "ran\nran\n" # so the test ran again

step unset: jet test
cwd: app
unset: TEST_READS_GREETING
exit: nonzero # the test fails without the variable
stderr: !~ "reused" # an unset variable differs from a set one
file: app/runs.log = "ran\nran\nran\n"
